nt"},"level":"2","description2":{"zh":"回合结束时，对自己和全体友方恢复20*n点形势值（n为我方总人数），该恢复形势值最高为60。","en":"At the end of the turn, restore 20*n Momentum to self and all allies (n = total allies). Max 60 Momentum restored."}}],"soulPoints":{"war":1500,"battle":500,"debate":6200},"equipment":[{"id":"WP1007902","name":{"zh":"文士羽扇","en":"Literati Feather Fan"},"level":"1","description":{"zh":"为才能杰出之人准备的小型羽扇。","en":"A compact feather fan prepared for persons of outstanding talent."},"atkVal":"3","mp":"120","price":"2000","slot":{"zh":"武器","en":"Weapon"}},{"id":"WP1014005","name":{"zh":"锦绣布衣·乙","en":"Embroidered Cloth Robe - II"},"level":"0","description":{"zh":"采用了普通的面料并进行了纹饰处理的布衣，衣服的边缘处也添加了简单的纹饰。","en":"A cloth garment made of ordinary fabric with decorative patterning, finished with simple trim along its edges."},"defenceVal":"2","mp":"340","price":"1200","slot":{"zh":"护甲","en":"Armor"}},{"id":"WP1024905","name":{"zh":"五梁冠·甲","en":"Five-Ridge Crown - I"},"level":"1","description":{"zh":"有五根横脊的礼冠，朝中官员最常见的冠帽之一，多在诸侯朝服时佩戴。","en":"A formal cap with five horizontal ridges, one of the most common caps among court officials, typically worn by lords with their court attire."},"defenceVal":"3","mp":"930","price":"4000","slot":{"zh":"头盔","en":"Helmet"}}],"family":{"children":{"label":{"zh":"子女","en":"Children"},"people":[{"id":"WJ10110","code":"100"},{"id":"WJ10461","code":"100"}]},"family":{"label":{"zh":"亲属","en":"Relatives"},"people":[{"id":"WJ10534","code":"100"}]}},"clans":[{"id":"GI106115","name":{"zh":"陇西辛氏","en":"The Xin clan of Longxi"},"years":["0","999"],"desc":{"zh":"出自姒姓，夏朝开国君主启封庶子于莘（今陕西合阳），后因音近改莘为辛，遂以辛为氏。其先祖本居陇西，东汉建武年间东迁至颍川阳翟（今河南禹州）。西汉时期，辛庆忌以功封营平侯，其子孙因受吕宽案牵连被诛杀，导致家族在东汉近二百年间沉寂无闻，直到三国时期才再度崛起。辛评、辛毗兄弟先仕袁绍，官渡之战后辛毗归曹，为曹操出谋划策，官至卫尉、侍中，封颍乡侯，位列九卿。其女辛宪英以才智闻名，预言钟会叛乱的结局。","en":"Originating from the Si surname, Qi, the founding Ruler of the Xia dynasty, enfeoffed his concubine-born son at Shen (modern-day Heyang, Shaanxi), which later evolved phonetically into Xin, becoming their clan name. Their ancestors originally resided in Longxi and migrated East to Yangzhai in Yingchuan (modern-day Yuzhou, Henan) during the Jianwu era of the Eastern Han. During the Western Han, Xin Qingji was enfeoffed as the Marquis of Yingping for his merit, but his descendants were executed due to implication in the Lu Kuan affair, leaving the clan in obscurity for nearly two hundred years throughout the Eastern Han until their resurgence in the Three Kingdoms period. The brothers Xin Ping and Xin Pi initially served Yuan Shao, after the Battle of Guandu, Xin Pi joined Cao Cao and served as a key strategist, rising to Commandant of the Guards and Attendant Palace Gentleman, enfeoffed as Marquis of Yingxiang and ranking among the Nine Ministers. His daughter Xin Xianying was famed for her wisdom, accurately predicting the outcome of Zhong Hui's rebellion."},"talent":{"military":"1","commerce":"5","politics":"7"}}],"friendGroups":[{"story":"S10802","members":["WJ10158","WJ10157","WJ10062","WJ10153","WJ10534"]},{"story":"S10802","members":["WJ10155","WJ10534","WJ10158","WJ10535"]},{"story":"S10615","members":["WJ10158","WJ10157","WJ10062","WJ10153","WJ10534"]},{"story":"S10615","members":["WJ10155","WJ10534","WJ10158","WJ10535"]},{"story":"S10402","members":["WJ10158","WJ10157","WJ10062","WJ10153","WJ10534"]},{"story":"S10402","members":["WJ10155","WJ10534","WJ10158","WJ10535"]},{"story":"S10402","members":["WJ10082","WJ10009","WJ10158","WJ10577","WJ10176","WJ10085","WJ10054","WJ10534","WJ10757","WJ10747","WJ10316"]},{"story":"S10415","members":["WJ10158","WJ10157","WJ10062","WJ10153","WJ10534"]},{"story":"S10415","members":["WJ10155","WJ10534","WJ10158","WJ10535"]},{"story":"S10415","members":["WJ10082","WJ10009","WJ10158","WJ10577","WJ10176","WJ10085","WJ10054","WJ10747","WJ10757","WJ10534","WJ10316"]},{"story":"S10202","members":["WJ10158","WJ10157","WJ10062","WJ10153","WJ10534","WJ10060"]},{"story":"S10202","members":["WJ10155","WJ10534","WJ10158","WJ10535"]},{"story":"S10202"